This file is never woven.  It holds one small program per test case of
[[countdown.py]]'s [[tests]] program in contents.nw, so that the deck
can show, beside each test case, what those lines print (didactic's
[[\runpython]]).  The test lines themselves are written once, as named
chunks in contents.nw; the programs here only reference them, and the
Makefile tangles them with both files (notangle concatenates the chunk
definitions of all its input files).

The test cases of [[countdown.py]] build no objects and depend on no
earlier case, so each program imports the function it tests and runs
only its own case.

The programs live here and not in contents.nw because a root woven
there would either print the harness chunks in the notes, or, hidden,
leave the test chunks' \enquote{used in} references pointing at labels
that do not exist.

